{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5201) titled \"[stitch] cmd/uname: help, version, and diagnostics (srd044-uname R4.1-R4.3)\". The task requires implementing SRD requirements R4.1, R4.2, and R4.3 for the uname utility, which focus on comprehensive differential testing. Specifically:\n   - R4.1: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (guname) via pkg/testutils\n   - R4.2: Tests must cover: default (no flags), each individual flag (-s, -n, -r, -v, -m, -p, -i, -o), -a, combinations of flags, and error cases\n   - R4.3: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment\n   \n   The task also requires adding differential test cases for these requirements and ensuring the code compiles and all tests pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (guname)\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests for test harness\n   - pkg/testutils.BuildBinary for building the Go binary under test\n   - exec.LookPath(\"guname\") with t.Skip for graceful skip when reference binary is absent\n   - DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, ExitCode, Normalize fields\n   - NormalizeFunc for normalizing binary name paths in error messages\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for consistent cross-platform behavior\n   - SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Manual flag parsing (not cobra) with support for --help, --version, short flags (-s, -n, etc.)\n   - unix.Uname syscall via golang.org/x/sys/unix\n   - The cobbler orchestrator manages git externally - no git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd044-uname.ya